  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>74</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Lanthanoids have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> oxidation state as stable&nbsp;oxidation state. Hence, in their&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;oxidation state, they act as an oxidising agents and&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;oxidation state, they act as reducing agents.</p></blockquote>",
